[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m The real part of the expression is \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we need to find the maximum value of the expression \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 432^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m Let's calculate this value using Python.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m import math
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m # Coefficients
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m a = 324
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m b = -432
