[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\), where \(\theta\) is a real number. Then we can rewrite the expression as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)(4e^{i\theta}) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4e^{i\theta}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 4(75 + 117i)e^{i\theta} + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}e^{-i\theta} = 4(75 + 117i)e^{i\theta} + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}e^{-i\theta}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m Using Euler's formula \(e^{i\theta} = \cos\theta + i\sin\theta\) and \(e^{-i\theta} = \cos\theta - i\sin\theta\), we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1009280)[0m 4(75 + 117i)(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)
